{"kind":"request","text":"Builder: deliver the focused portable numeric-conversion decision amendment requested by Hugh under #4242, before the corresponding I7 runtime change.\n\nThe [current capability-context note](notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md@62fde5411d74317d32e56b6d9b0bc1f0c62b4142:509) is published by artifact #4246 (a1c97964) after the approved object-key amendment landed at main 62fde541. Use that current source. Keep this a concise amendment: one explicit rule, the changed/unchanged cases and references to the existing shared gates. Put the complete conversion inventory and executable controls in signed attachments. Runtime, evaluator pin and callers remain on original #4043.\n\nThe attached native probe/results and compiler summary are Hugh's independent observations at pinned599f/Go1.26.7 ARM and exact private311d compiled for four targets. Original Builder evidence remains at #4236; the expanded40-case survey remains at #4239. These establish a compatibility decision to make; they do not claim AMD64 evaluator execution or a completed physical bound proof.","body":{"branch":"request/i7-numeric-conversion-decision","conditions":"Deliver a source-only amendment to notes/2026-09-05-capability-context-contract.md in a new request/i7-numeric-conversion-decision worktree/branch from then-current main, after object-key source #4228 lands. Preserve all adopted callable/group/tuple/object-key decisions. Publish the exact candidate and an ordinary proposal; Hugh must ratify that exact proposal before independent Checker Architecture/Security/Simplification review. Builder then ratifies the exact approval, seals/pushes with correct path succession, verifies main CI and removes the owned worktree/branch. Do not rewrite an adopted exact head merely to replace historical pending-adoption wording. No runtime change belongs on this source child.\n\nProposed governing choice for exact adoption: define one architecture-independent signed64 numeric conversion for reachable float-to-index/precision casts. NaN maps to zero. A value at or above exact positive 2^63, including positive infinity, maps to MaxInt64; a value at or below exact negative 2^63, including negative infinity, maps to MinInt64. All other finite values truncate toward zero. Compare against exactly representable powers of two before a native cast; float64(MaxInt64) rounds to 2^63 and is not an inclusive safe conversion bound. Preserve negative zero and finite fractional behavior. This is a deliberate portable language rule matching the observed ARM baseline; disclose changed AMD64 behavior rather than pretending it is already portable pinned semantics. No runtime architecture branch, silent AMD64 selection, blanket nonfinite rejection or automatic widening of the admitted builtin set.\n\nKeep operation-specific behavior and evaluation/error ordering after conversion. Specify signed64 arithmetic, including the existing defined wrap behavior at downstream substring bounds and decimal-exponent arithmetic where it affects results; four supported targets are 64-bit. Keep the existing protected failure/refusal for invalid substring slices without allowing a host panic, changing a failure into a successful empty result or introducing an unrelated global refusal. Explicitly cover $round(1.25,0/0): portable result1 versus masked-Intel inference0; substring(\"abc\",0,1e300): portable \"abc\" versus inferred empty; substring(\"abc\",1,1e300): retained failure versus inferred empty. Cover +/-infinity, +/-huge finite values, signed64 boundaries and nearest representable neighbors, negative zero, fractional precision/start/length, huge exponent arithmetic, missing/undefined and empty string behavior. State exact output or existing error class; runtime-derived diagnostic text is not a portable success criterion.\n\nDo not apply this rule to every floating intermediate or every Go cast. Preserve predicate semantics, including pinned [1,2,3][0/0] retaining all items, infinity's existing D1001 refusal, finite out-of-input indices selecting nothing and floor-before-index behavior. Inventory every reachable numeric-to-integer/index/precision conversion under the complete admitted AST/callable subset, including aliases/partials and internal helper paths. For each identify whether this rule applies or prove an earlier type/range/length bound makes conversion portable. Three identified builtin sites (round precision and substring start/length) are starting evidence, not a completeness claim. Existing nonfinite input/output/value-graph gates remain unchanged; nonfinite intermediates are addressed at their semantic conversion point only. Excluded builtin casts need an explicit reachability reason, not an assumed grep result.\n\nRetain exact pinned and private native observations, the explicit controlled-overlay comparisons and primary instruction evidence separately. Hugh independently compiled exact311d with Go1.26.7 for darwin/linux x arm64/amd64 and observed FCVTZSD versus CVTTSD2SQ at round precision; Intel SDM table D-8 establishes the masked NaN integer-indefinite conversion. This is instruction-level proof under the stated floating exception assumption, not execution on AMD64 or full host replay. The decision may rely on that declared evidence, but full #4043 still owes cross-target evidence and the complete four-build physical proof before admission. Give executable paired old/new output/error/ordered-call/work/allocation controls; require equal deterministic accounting for equal portable semantics across targets, actual at-bound/one-over outcomes, and omission controls that restore a native cast, miss a guard or remove a relevant charge. Reuse the40-case survey and24-case independent controls as seeds, not as a substitute for complete coverage.\n\nAccount for the semantic change in existing core.jsonata, grammar/dialect and corpus/version identity components wherever affected; retain exactly ten components and old-identity recognition. Revalidate stored programs before replay writes, with refusal leaving projection and frontier unchanged. Preserve acknowledged reset/activation and all four stages/eight gates. This child authorizes no public evaluator/module publication, production admission, live host operation, reset, migration or release. The original full #4043 commitment remains open for implementation, eventual pin and all callers. Current behavior descriptions must rest on their actual live implementation artifacts; retain meaningful provenance even if ordinary staleness persists. Verify owning-head source and evidence previews and local links. Run checks proportionate to this documentation-only change; do not add wording-only tests or rerun unrelated suites.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:56e334a3fa48a41186bf93e84791fc33402d664d stale; retired bases: git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:727ab6a7638f58a47794d38e316d240f06ccc55f, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:8c17d9e03de8cacb255a59d1859dc84ef6f78c70, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:dbff4da89a2356475801f4e736c4c173e1258f14","target_head":"62fde5411d74317d32e56b6d9b0bc1f0c62b4142","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f","to":"00721374a520eabbbd4ded64dd018110f47545ff20112bee83c75f478e15f818"}}